  "title": "The knot's three-fold spaces are Fano atoms in planar glue",
  "subject": "The connected 3-regular triple systems that resist 2-colouring, read as the knot's three-fold spaces",
  "conclusion": "Every such system other than the Fano plane contains at least two Fano planes with one element removed, attached by three-edge cuts; everything else is planar Pfaffian glue (doubled squares, planar braces, and trisums built from them), and every planar cubic bipartite graph occurs as glue. The approved grammar of splices and odd cycles was incomplete: a 43-point system has the cube as glue.",
